   33	 * The account works on one ambition at a time: the cheapest thing it cannot yet produce. Satisfying
   34	 * the union of every ambition's prerequisites instead is a ladder with no top -- the catalogue always
   35	 * names one more deep unlock, so the chain never finishes, the economy never gets a turn, and the
   36	 * account ends the day with a level-seven shipyard standing over level-three mines. A player picks a
   37	 * goal, stands what it needs, and goes back to mining; the next goal gets its turn on a later
   38	 * session, and the economy ranks in between.
